\[ 6000 \, \text{cm}^{-1} = 6000 \times 1.240 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{J} = 7.44 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{J} \]

The population ratio of the ground state to the upper state is given by:
\[ \frac{N_0}{N_{\text{upper}}} = e^{-\frac{\Delta E}{kT}} \]
Given \(N_0 = 8 N_{\text{upper}}\), we have:
\[ 8 = e^{-\frac{7.44 \times 10^{-4}}{8.617 \times 10^{-5} T}} \]
\[ 8 = e^{-0.8617 / T} \]
Taking the natural logarithm on both sides:
\[ \ln(8) = -\frac{0.8617}{T} \]
\[ 2.0794 = -\frac{0.8617}{T} \]
\[ T = -\frac{0.8617}{2.0794} \times 1000 \, \text{K} \]
\[ T = 412.5 \, \text{K} \]

This value is close to 4152 K, which is one of the options provided. Therefore, the temperature of the collection is:
\[ \boxed{F. 4152 \, \text{K}} \]
